    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d415">

                <pb facs="0518" n="508" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg508"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.796/7–1544: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-15T22:00:00-04:00">July 15, 1944—10
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5582. Please deliver the following message to Lord Beaverbrook from Assistant
                    Secretary Berle: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In view of your approaching visit to this country,<anchor n="52"
                                xml:id="d415-f1"/> I wonder if it would be convenient for you to
                            take this opportunity to continue the exploratory talks on civil
                            aviation which Warner and I commenced in London. We have made
                            considerable progress in our talks with representatives of other nations
                            and are most anxious to explore further with you various points on which
                            there still may be some disparity in our views. If this suggestion is
                            agreeable to you, I presume you will wish to bring some of your
                            technical advisers, and I assure you we shall be most happy to receive
                            them as well as yourself.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>If the above invitation is accepted, we should like to have Satterthwaite proceed
                    to Washington to be present throughout the discussions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d415-f1" n="52" xml:id="d415-f1-content">
                <p>Regarding Lord Beaverbrook’s visit to the United States to discuss matters
                    relating to petroleum, see <ref target="frus1944v03#pg_94">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp. 94</ref>, <ref
                        target="frus1944v03#pg_118">118</ref>–<ref target="frus1944v03#pg_121"
                        >121</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
